problems, the C file system includes the function feof( ), which determines when the
end of the file has been encountered. The feof( ) function has this prototype:
int feof(FILE *fp);
feof( ) returns true if the end of the file has been reached; otherwise, it returns 0.
Therefore, the following routine reads a binary file until the end of the file is
encountered:
while(!feof(fp)) ch = getc(fp);
